  "problem": "$\\,$ $2\u2223x$\n\nThe predicate $P(x)$ is given above. Which of following represents $\u00acP(x)?$",
  "worked_solution": "In plain English, our predicate $P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $2$ divides $x.$\n\nThe symbol \"$\u00ac$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $2$ divides $x$, \n\nIn other words, $2$ does not divide $x.$ Therefore, $\u00acP(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $2\u2224x$",
